# Memory — a concrete PERSISTENCE adapter that keeps an aggregate's repository
# in an in-process HashMap : no disk, discarded on shutdown. The sibling of Heki
# on the SAME persistence family — same `persisted_by` verb, same reply signal,
# distinct backing. It DECLARES the family it implements (the inverted arrow) ;
# the family never names it.
#
# The bind `SomeDomain::Agg.persisted_by("Memory")` resolves IFF Memory's
# declared family (persistence) carries `persisted_by` — the same typed attach
# checkpoint Heki passes. Memory carries NO per-deployment values (no location
# to configure), so unlike Heki it has no matching .world block : the bind alone
# is the whole wiring. This is the adapter the conception's ephemeral / compute /
# pure-projection domains bind, declaring them transient on purpose rather than
# riding the heki default by accident.
Hecks.adapter "Memory" do
  family "persistence"
end
